@*
    Catch-all host page. It exists so that EVERY url matches a Razor component endpoint and the
    host document above is rendered for it; from there Bit.Brouter's <AppRouter /> - rendered by
    Routes.razor in the client project - takes over and matches the real route. Brouter matches
    during OnInitializedAsync, so the matched page's HTML is in the initial prerendered response.

    It deliberately lives in the Server project: the client assembly is Brouter's AppAssembly, and
    a "/{*path}" @page in there would be picked up by Brouter's own attribute-route discovery.
*@
@page "/"
@page "/{*path}"

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Path { get; set; }
}
